
/*
    TinyCraft VM demo v59 performance recovery
    Based on packed-cache TinyCraft branch
    -----------------
    Minecraft-like voxel prototype for the RP2350/Pico VM Tiny-C compiler.

    Controls use common PS/2 Set-2 scancodes:
        W/S         move forward / backward
        A/D         strafe left / right
        I/K         camera look up / down, all the way vertical
        J/L         camera turn left / right
        Space       smooth one-block jump
        Shift       run
        Hold Z      mine blocks over time, or swing if no block is targeted
        X           place equipped hotbar block with a short pitch animation
        1..9        select equipped hotbar slot
        E           open/close inventory
        M           pause menu
        Inventory/menu cursor mode:
                    I/J/K/L moves cursor
                    A = left click, D = right click
                    movement/camera keys are disabled while cursor mode is active


    v59 performance recovery:
        - opaque and masked VM rasterizers no longer share transparency work
        - entity collisions run on a fixed physics cadence instead of every rendered frame
        - interpolated mob rotations use cached tick endpoints instead of per-frame trigonometry
        - entity definitions and per-part texture bindings are reused while unchanged

    v58 masked block-breaking texture patch:
        - TCAC v8 carries ten environment destroy-stage textures and 1-bit masks in one record
        - block breaking uses the native masked textured-quad builtin on exposed faces
        - destroy-stage assets use dedicated arrays and do not consume general texture IDs

    v53 block/model/entity definition asset records:
        - TCAC v8 can carry compact runtime block, block-model, entity, and entity-model records
        - block hardness, drops, tool rules, texture IDs, item links, and behavior flags can load from assets.tca
        - old compiled block definitions are only used as a no-block-record fallback

    v64 flat item texture mesh patch:
        - TCAC v3+ texture records can carry a 1-bit alpha mask after RGB332 pixels
        - PC asset packer can generate flat item meshes from item PNG alpha
        - non-block item UI icons use asset-cache item textures and masks
        - flat item meshes stay data-driven in assets.tca, not hardcoded in source

    v63 custom mesh item cache patch:
        - TCAC v2 can carry baked custom mesh item records beside texture records
        - runtime stores compact item mesh face tables loaded from assets.tca
        - item records can switch to TC_ITEM_RENDER_CUSTOM_MESH without JSON parsing during gameplay
        - first-person held items can render cache-loaded custom mesh faces

    v62 relative package folder patch:
        - runtime save/config/asset paths are local filenames inside the launched folder
        - the deployable game folder is Tinycraft/ with the binary beside config/assets/worlds
        - converter defaults to writing assets.tca inside that Tinycraft folder
        - the VM runtime patch resolves relative SD paths against the launched program folder

    v61 external asset converter patch:
        - adds a PC-side asset packer under the versioned tools folder
        - converter accepts PNG plus raw .rgb332/.rg332 texture sources
        - initial converter wrote assets.tca in the existing TCAC v1 format
        - documents editable manifests and the current runtime cache limits

    v60 binary asset cache patch:
        - adds startup loading for assets.tca
        - cache records can override baked texture registry slots with raw RGB332 data
        - block textures load into 16x16 cache slots, entity atlases load into fixed 64x32 slots
        - baked textures remain the fallback when the cache file is missing or invalid

    v59 block registry patch:
        - block registration is split into src/03_block_registry.tc
        - BlockDef now carries linked item ID and behavior flags
        - built-in blocks are registered through the block registry before item generation
        - old runtime block helpers now route through registry-owned metadata

    v58 item registry patch:
        - item registration is split into src/02_item_registry.tc
        - items now carry use-action and behavior flags for startup-loaded metadata
        - block items are generated from registered block definitions
        - old runtimeItem helpers now route through the item registry

    v57 texture registry patch:
        - baked textures are registered once at startup with metadata and stable IDs
        - block/item/runtime lookups now resolve texture IDs through the registry
        - entity texture metadata is registered too, ready for later SD/cache loading

    v54 pig polish/collision patch:
        - snout moved one pixel lower on the face
        - hind legs and their pivots moved two pixels toward the rear
        - small text uses per-glyph width plus one-pixel spacing
        - pigs use AABB overlap pushes against the player/other pigs and a larger block hitbox

    v57 runtime table foundation:
        - block/item behavior now flows through BlockDef and ItemDef runtime tables
        - no SD asset loading yet; built-in definitions are baked at startup

    v53 pig UV/hand rollback patch:
        - pig cuboid UVs use full pixel-panel spans instead of size-minus-one spans
        - removes the 2D hand overlay pass and returns to the 3D viewmodel only

    v53 atlas/font repair patch:
        - pig atlas is regenerated from C:/Users/enzob/Downloads/pig.png
        - pig UVs use exact clamped texel coordinates without the inset workaround
        - UI glyph table is generated from the 16x16 8x8-cell ascii.png sheet

    v53 entity/config/font patch:
        - config.txt is line-based, human-readable, and editable
        - E opens inventory; render distance is changed from the settings menu
        - pig state uses struct Pig slots and streams through the world .tcw entity section
        - fixes empty/corrupt entity sections respawning no pigs after load
        - pigs push the player as well as themselves when AABBs overlap
        - pig head yaw/pitch uses smooth look-control clamps and render interpolation
        - first-person hand gets a depthless overlay pass above terrain and below HUD

    v53 skylight horizontal-bleed patch:
        - raw sky light now bleeds sideways from nearby open-sky columns with Minecraft-style taxicab falloff
        - a single opaque block overhead no longer forces sky light to zero if adjacent open air can feed light underneath

    v53 sky-darkening/gameplay-light patch:
        - open-sky technical sky light remains 15, but effective gameplay sky light applies a day/night darkening value
        - sunset lowers effective open-sky light from 14 to 4, night holds at 4, sunrise returns to 15
        - added future hostile-mob light helper: at night it checks block light only and ignores sky light
        - T overlay now shows darkening plus effective sky/block/total light

    v53 pig passive AI / light-level patch:
        - pig wandering now uses rest/walk-to-target behavior
        - pig legs rotate around their model pivots
        - added math-only block/sky light level helpers and T overlay display
        - pig spawning now requires grass, clearance and light >= 7

    v42 pig AI/performance optimization:
        - pig AI now runs on a slower fixed mob tick instead of every frame
        - pig terrain/collision checks are skipped while still inside the same block
        - cached pig sin/cos and leg animation values reduce per-frame trig work
        - far pigs use a cheaper body/head-only render LOD

    v41 pig render/orientation fix:
        - pig movement vector now matches the rendered local -Z forward axis
        - body texture mapping handles the Bedrock 90-degree body bind rotation


    v40 pig movement polish:
        - pig yaw now smoothly turns toward a target direction instead of snapping
        - random wandering uses small continuous angle changes, not 45/90 degree steps
        - obstacle avoidance picks a new target yaw but still rotates gradually

    v39 pig mob prototype:
        - adds simple wandering pig mobs rendered from the uploaded pig model/texture
        - pigs use textured cuboids, terrain-following movement, and basic wall collision

    v38 dynamic terrain-height rendering fix:
        - natural render/loading now computes each 8x8 render chunk's highest
          procedural terrain/tree block and builds sections up to that height
        - removes the hard-coded section 0..4 natural terrain limit

    v37 movement smoothing fix:
        - acceleration/drag/gravity still run only on 50 ms physics ticks
        - player position is smoothed every rendered frame again

    v36 gameplay fixes:
        - manually dropped hotbar items have a 2 second pickup cooldown
        - spawn uses natural terrain instead of a forced flat plateau
        - dropped items collide horizontally with solid blocks
        - thrown item direction follows camera pitch more strongly
        - low-FPS jump catch-up uses fixed 50 ms physics ticks only

    v35 UI font consistency:
        - inventory item names and stack counts now use the same 5x7 style as the menu

    v23 sky sun + grass_carried changes:
        - sun is now real 3D sky geometry instead of a HUD rectangle
        - grass top texture uses blocks/grass_carried.png

    v21 packed far-render cache changes:
        - render distance > 1 uses a compact one-word-per-column cache
        - no procedural tree/terrain calls happen in the far per-frame hot loop
        - far block drawing inlines packed neighbor checks and face submission

    v14 procedural world changes:
        - world[] is now a 16x8x16 active chunk/window around the player
        - world_origin_x/world_origin_z convert local block coords to absolute coords
        - terrain is generated deterministically from seed + absolute coordinates
        - broken/placed blocks are stored in a small global edit overlay
        - when the player moves near an edge, the active window recenters and regenerates
        Hold Z      mine/break first block under the crosshair over time
        X           place equipped hotbar block on the face under the crosshair
        1..9        select hotbar slot; E opens the 3x9 inventory

    If your keyboard firmware uses different scancodes, change the integer
    literals in updatePlayer(). The current compiler requires key() scancodes
    to be integer literals.
*/

// v24 changes:
// - builds a greedy mesh from the packed face cache when the render cache rebuilds
// - renders merged real-3D quads with fillQuad3DTexZTiled() so large faces repeat textures
// - indexes greedy meshes by 8x8 render chunk so each frame walks only visible chunks
// - shows FPS by default; press T to cycle FPS / XYZ coordinates / VM render stats
// - draws chunks near-to-far, pre-culls off-frustum chunks, and skips back-facing block faces
// - groups each chunk's greedy mesh by face direction so nearer face buckets draw first
// - skips off-screen sun quads and uses tighter chunk frustum margins for sky views
// - keeps v23 intact by living in this new tinycraft_v24.tc file


    /*v42 tighter culling + pig step patch:
        - render chunks touched this frame are stamped so pigs only draw in actually rendered x/z chunks
        - object/chunk frustum culling uses tighter horizontal/vertical projection limits
        - drops, sky bodies, stars, clouds and pigs stop drawing as soon as their bounds leave the view
        - pig movement tries one-block step-up when the body footprint hits a ledge and walks off one-block drops cleanly
        - pig turning speed increased to reduce the minimum turning radius

    v41 pig AI/gravity + culling patch:
        - pigs keep vertical physics even while resting, so broken floor blocks make them fall
        - pig walk goals no longer require spawn light, only valid floor/clearance
        - pigs render only if their terrain render chunk is loaded and the pig is inside the camera frustum
        - sun, moon, stars and cloud quads now skip drawing when off-screen
        - T overlay light calculation is cached briefly to avoid repeated skylight-bleed scans*/

/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* Tunable globals/constants. Keep these global so the VM stack stays small.  */
/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------- */

/* The VM texture path behaves best at the same coordinate scale used by the
   reference demo. Physics/collision remains in voxel units, but rendering and
   camera coordinates are multiplied by block_world_size. */
float block_world_size = 1024.0f;
float texel_max = 15.0f;

/* Block IDs. Keep IDs below 16 because the packed render cache stores
   one block in four bits. */
uint BLOCK_AIR = 0;
uint BLOCK_GRASS = 1;
uint BLOCK_DIRT = 2;
uint BLOCK_STONE = 3;
uint BLOCK_WOOD = 4;
uint BLOCK_LEAVES = 5;
uint BLOCK_OAK_PLANKS = 6;
uint BLOCK_CRAFTING_TABLE = 7;
uint BLOCK_COBBLESTONE = 8;

/* Non-placeable item IDs. These stay above the packed block range, so the
   world/cache can still store real blocks in 4 bits per cell. */
